<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Taifa of Valencia</h1><p class="st-meta">1010 CE – 1094 CE (approx.) · capital Valencia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A rich taifa on the Valencian huerta, governed by Amirid heirs and later by Toledo, whose fall ended with El Cid's conquest of the city in 1094.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1010-1011 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freedmen">freedmen</a> Mubarak and Muzaffar took control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/caliphate-of-cordoba">Caliphate of Córdoba</a> disintegrated. In 1021 the city recognised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-aziz-ibn-abi-amir">Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Amir</a>, a grandson of the regent al-Mansur, whose family ruled until 1065.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a> drew wealth from irrigated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huerta">huerta</a> farming, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> and its port. Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-aziz">al-Aziz</a> (1021-1061) was a capable ruler who also controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a> for a time. In 1065 al-Mamun of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/taifa-of-toledo">Taifa of Toledo</a> annexed the city, and after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> fell in 1085 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI</a> installed the deposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yahya-al-qadir">al-Qadir</a> in Valencia as a Castilian client.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1092 the qadi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-jahhaf">Ibn Jahhaf</a> killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yahya-al-qadir">al-Qadir</a> and appealed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-cid">Rodrigo Díaz</a>, El Cid, besieged the city and took it in June 1094, creating the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-valencia">Lordship of Valencia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/taifa-of-valencia.jpg" alt="Taifa of Valencia" width="320" height="271"><figcaption>Image: Tyk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Location_map_Taifa_of_Valencia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1010 CE – 1094 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Valencia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Amir, Abd al-Malik al-Muzaffar, Yahya al-Qadir</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic, Mozarabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Valencia (taifa)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1052&amp;focus=taifa-of-valencia" aria-label="Taifa of Valencia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4671 764 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Taifa of Valencia lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4991 1020L4881 1071M4991 1020L4901 1007M4991 1020L4991 1020"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4881 1071h0M4901 1007h0M4991 1020h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4991 1020h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4991 1020h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1052&amp;focus=taifa-of-valencia">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
